# SaveProof — project context

## What we are building
SaveProof turns an Indian MSME factory's energy data (DISCOM bills or 15-min meter data) plus production records into **verified energy savings with an uncertainty band**, delivered as an MRV report that a BEE-certified energy auditor reviews and signs.
- Competition: Schneider Electric Yuva Yodha, Challenge 4 (Smart Manufacturing). Prototype due **22 Nov 2026**; we submit **20 Nov**.
- Primary user: the BEE-empanelled energy auditor doing ADEETIE MRV. Secondary: MSME owner, lender.
- Why it matters: ADEETIE pays interest subvention only if ≥10% energy savings are achieved and sustained. A naive before/after bill comparison, or BEE's SEC-ratio formula, misreads savings whenever production changes.

## In scope
1. Baseline model: daily/monthly kWh ~ production + operating days (+ day type), fitted on the baseline period only.
2. Verified savings + uncertainty band (ASHRAE Guideline 14 statistics) and an ADEETIE verdict.
3. Comparators: naive bill comparison and BEE SEC-ratio.
4. Three validation experiments: null test, injected saving, blind simulator test.
5. Data quality score; CUSUM drift alarm.
6. Streamlit app + 1–2 page MRV report PDF (with CO₂).

## Out of scope (don't build unless asked)
Auth, databases, user accounts, Docker, cloud infra, real hardware, OCR for many bill formats, Tally/ERP integration, multi-language UI, lender portal, weather models, ML beyond one optional comparison.

## Cut order if late
Modbus meter simulator → bill parser → drift UI → dashboard polish. Never cut: engine, the three experiments, MRV report.

## Stack (don't add to it without asking)
Python 3.11+, pandas, numpy, statsmodels, scipy, matplotlib, streamlit, reportlab, pytest, ruff. Optional stretch: pymodbus.

