## Data contract — the one table every layer speaks
One row per period (day, month or billing cycle):

| column | type | notes |
|---|---|---|
| period_start, period_end | datetime64, midnight, plant-local; end inclusive | bills are irregular — never assume calendar months |
| kwh | float ≥ 0 | energy consumed in the period |
| production | float ≥ 0, nullable | output quantity |
| production_unit | str | t, pcs, m, kL, or `proxy:<name>` when it isn't a real quantity |
| operating_days | float | days the plant actually ran in the period |
| source | str | `real_meter`, `utility_bill`, `simulated` |
| dataset | str | e.g. `uci_steel`, `irish_mi_a`, `sim_foundry_007` |
| coverage_pct | float 0–100 | share of expected readings present |
| event | str, nullable | `retrofit`, `shutdown`, `meter_fault`, `holiday` |

Optional bill columns: `kvah`, `max_demand_kva`, `power_factor`.
Plant metadata travels separately (dataclass): plant_id, sector, timezone, retrofit_date, baseline and reporting period dates.

